---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const required = `schema, tool_version, task_ids, checks_run, budget, seed,
findings, coverage, started_at, duration_s`;
---

<Docs
  current="report"
  title="Report format"
  description="The aethens-report/v2 JSON schema and the Markdown report that aethens audit can write."
>
  <p class="kicker mb-5"><span>Docs</span><span class="num" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Report</span></p>
  <h1 class="font-serif italic font-semibold text-section leading-[1.1]">Report format</h1>
  <p class="mt-6 text-paper/90">
    <code class="text-gold">aethens audit --format json</code> writes a report that
    follows <code class="text-gold">aethens-report/v2</code>. The formal schema is
    <a class="prose-link" href="https://github.com/beastrog/aethens/blob/main/docs/report-schema.json">docs/report-schema.json</a>.
    JSON is the CLI default. <code class="text-gold">--format markdown</code>
    renders the same report as Markdown sized for a pull-request comment. The
    GitHub Action always writes Markdown to
    <code class="text-gold">aethens-report.md</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="top-level" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">Top-level fields</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    Required fields, in schema order:
  </p>
  <pre class="cmd mt-4" tabindex="0"><code>{required}</code></pre>
  <div class="scroll-x mt-6">
    <table class="sheet">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Field</th>
          <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>schema</code></td>
          <td>The constant <code>aethens-report/v2</code>. v2 adds <code>coverage</code>; v1 reports had no coverage list but still load.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>tool_version</code></td>
          <td>The Aethens version that produced the report.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>task_ids</code></td>
          <td>The task ids included in the run.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>checks_run</code></td>
          <td>Check ids of the form <code>C000</code>, for example C001–C007.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>budget</code></td>
          <td><code>smoke</code>, <code>standard</code>, or <code>deep</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>seed</code></td>
          <td>Integer seed used for the run.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>started_at</code></td>
          <td>ISO 8601 timestamp with a UTC offset.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>duration_s</code></td>
          <td>Run duration in seconds, at least 0.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>findings</code></td>
          <td>The list of findings. Additional properties on the report object are not allowed.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>coverage</code></td>
          <td>Statements a check can make where it found nothing, for example C002’s flake-rate bound.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="finding" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">A finding</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    Every finding has these required fields:
    <code class="text-gold">id</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">check_id</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">severity</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">task_id</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">title</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">detail</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">evidence</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">repro</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">seed</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">confidence</code>, and
    <code class="text-gold">limits</code>.
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-paper/90">
    <li><code class="text-gold">severity</code> is <code>error</code>, <code>warning</code>, or <code>info</code>.</li>
    <li><code class="text-gold">confidence</code> is <code>confirmed</code> or <code>needs-review</code>.</li>
    <li><code class="text-gold">repro</code> is a one-line command that reproduces the finding.</li>
    <li><code class="text-gold">limits</code> records what the check did and did not try.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="evidence" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">Evidence</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    Each finding’s <code class="text-gold">evidence</code> object has
    <code class="text-gold">subject</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">command</code> (an argument list),
    <code class="text-gold">observed</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">exit_codes</code> (integers or null),
    <code class="text-gold">timed_out</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">stdout_tail</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">stderr_tail</code>, and
    <code class="text-gold">extra</code> (a string-to-string map).
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    <code class="text-gold">subject</code> is one of
    <code class="text-gold">starter</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">gold</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">candidate:&lt;name&gt;</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">mutant:&lt;key&gt;</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">test:&lt;id&gt;</code> (C005),
    <code class="text-gold">rewrite:&lt;family&gt;</code> (C006), or
    <code class="text-gold">probe:&lt;category&gt;</code> (C007).
  </p>

  <h2 id="coverage" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">Coverage</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    A coverage entry has <code class="text-gold">check_id</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">task_id</code>,
    <code class="text-gold">statement</code>, and
    <code class="text-gold">stats</code> (a string-to-string map). It records
    something a check can say even though it found nothing, for example C002:
    flake rate below p at 95% confidence, or a C004 equivalent mutant that was
    not reported.
  </p>

  <h2 id="markdown" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">Markdown reports</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    A Markdown report starts with the heading “Aethens report”, then a line with
    the tool version, budget, seed, checks run, task count, and duration, then a
    count of error, warning, and info findings.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    If there are no findings, it says: “No findings. This only means the checks
    listed above found nothing at this budget and seed; it is not a guarantee
    about the verifier.”
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    If there are findings, it prints a summary table (severity, check, task,
    title), then a details block for each finding with the observed result,
    subject, confidence, seed, command, limits, the repro command, and output
    tails when present. Findings are ordered by severity (error, then warning,
    then info), task id, check id, and finding id. A closing note reminds
    readers that C004 info findings may be semantically equivalent to the gold,
    and that findings rely on what was run.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    If the coverage list is not empty, a “Coverage (what was established where
    nothing was found)” table follows, with check, task, and statement columns.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-muted">
    Sources: <a class="prose-link" href="https://github.com/beastrog/aethens/blob/main/docs/report-schema.json">docs/report-schema.json</a>
    and <code>src/aethens/report.py</code>. See also
    <a class="prose-link" href={`${base}docs/checks/`}>the checks</a> and
    <a class="prose-link" href={`${base}docs/cli/`}>the CLI</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
